  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The strip is accordion folded to form 16 pages (8 panels), each containing a map and a removable card held in place by tabs. Issued in paper slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Title from slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Chronicles of Migration invites viewer participation in order to create narrative content. This accordion book contains 16 extractable image cards, which, when removed, reveal a series of questions (Who, What, Where, etc.). The reader/viewer is prompted to reorganize and interpret the image cards, according to the questions, 'to tell the story or stories about migration, historic or contemporary'. The collaged images are intentionally both specific and broad so that a range of interpretations might be evoked. There is no right or wrong way to 'tell the story'. Rather, the project seeks to stimulate thoughts and ideas about this crucial topic."--Artist's statement from Vamp &amp; Tramp Booksellers website, viewed January 21, 2017.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Organize the cards in order to tell the story or stories about migration, historic or contemporary."--Slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
